course: dictionary
lesson: 15173
title: Scrubbed: clean or cancelled?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Scrubbed is the past form of scrub, which means to clean something by rubbing it hard, often with a brush, soap and water. «Mia scrubbed the muddy football boots until they shone.» The boots were muddy, and until they shone tells you Mia rubbed them hard to get them clean.
explain: Scrubbed can also mean cancelled. «The rocket launch was scrubbed because of strong winds.» Nobody rubbed the rocket. The launch was called off. Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: «The rocket launch was cancelled because of strong winds» still makes sense, so cancelled is the right meaning here.
explain: Context is the key. Look at the words around scrubbed. Boots, soap and muddy suggest cleaning. A launch, a rocket and winds suggest a plan that did not go ahead.
fact: Scrub is a verb, and scrubbed is its past form: scrub, scrubs, scrubbed, scrubbing.
fact: «Scrubbed» can mean very clean after scrubbing, as in «The kitchen was scrubbed clean.»
fact: «Scrubbed» can also mean cancelled, as in «The launch was scrubbed».
fact: Phrases to know include «scrubbed the floor» and «scrubbed up».
fact: Doctors scrub their hands before surgery to keep them clean.
exercise: «Sam scrubbed his knees after the football match.» What does scrubbed mean here? | Torn | Hidden | Painted | *Cleaned by rubbing hard
exercise: «The school trip was scrubbed because of the storm.» What does scrubbed mean here? | Finished early | *Cancelled | Enjoyed | Cleaned
exercise: Which form is the past of scrub? | *scrubbed | scrubs | scrub | scrubbing
test: «The kitchen was scrubbed clean before the party.» What does scrubbed clean mean? | *Very clean after scrubbing | Broken | Dirty and wet | Painted white
test: «The concert was scrubbed because the singer was ill.» What does scrubbed mean here? | Moved to a bigger hall | *Cancelled | Filmed | Cleaned with soap
exam: «The nurse scrubbed her hands before she touched the baby.» What does scrubbed mean in this sentence? | Hidden | Painted | *Cleaned hard with soap and water | Cancelled
